# Input spec for requirements-heavy.txt (the compiled lock).
#
# Superset of requirements-base.in plus the geo / ML / NLP / marketing-API
# packages. These are split out because they add roughly a gigabyte to the image
# and are needed by a small minority of DAGs — putting them in the default image
# would slow cold start for the ~28 gsheets notebooks that never touch them.
#
# Consumers (from dags/**/*_cluster.yml):
#   apache-sedona      → reverse_regions_polygon, ebdb_location, dw_datamarts_for_sale
#   scikit-learn       → enrich_lost_listings
#   lightgbm           → enrich_lost_listings
#   presidio-analyzer  → enrich_anonymization
#   spacy              → enrich_anonymization (also needs the en_core_web_lg model)
#   pytopojson         → reverse_regions_polygon
#   langfuse           → LLM tracing DAGs
#   facebook-business  → facebook_insights
#   google-ads         → growth marketing DAGs
#   acryl-datahub      → governance DAGs
#
# NOTE: the DAGs pin acryl-datahub==1.4.0, which requires Python >=3.10 and is
# therefore NOT installable on EMR 7.12's Python 3.9. The lock resolves to the
# newest 3.9-compatible release instead. If a notebook genuinely needs 1.4.0,
# that is a signal to move this image to Python 3.11 (available in EMR 7.12,
# default from 7.13) rather than to force it with --ignore-requires-python.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   make lock-emr-serverless-notebook

-r requirements-base.in

# --- heavy tier: geo / ML / NLP / marketing APIs ---
apache-sedona
scikit-learn>=0.24.0
lightgbm>=3.3.1
presidio-analyzer
spacy
pytopojson
langfuse
facebook-business
google-ads
acryl-datahub
